:R-HSA-69615  a             owl:NamedIndividual , obo:GO_0008150 ;
        rdfs:comment        "In the G1 phase there are two types of DNA damage responses, the p53-dependent and the p53-independent pathways. The p53-dependent responses inhibit CDKs through the up-regulation of genes encoding CKIs mediated by the p53 protein, whereas the p53-independent mechanisms inhibit CDKs through the inhibitory T14Y15 phosphorylation of Cdk2. Failure of DNA damage checkpoints in G1 leads to mutagenic replication of damaged templates and other replication defects." ;
        rdfs:label          "G1/S DNA Damage Checkpoints" ;
        dc:contributor      "Authored: Hoffmann, I, Khanna, K, 2003-06-05 08:03:42" , "GOC:reactome_curators" ;
        dc:date             "2023-06-21" ;
        pav:providedBy      "https://reactome.org" ;
